# CEO's OS — Prompt Discipline

## Purpose

Obligate structured execution. Prevent improvisation, placeholder patches, silent scope creep, and undocumented reasoning.

Every agent working on CEO's OS must show what it will touch, what it will not touch, and how it will validate before and after changes.

## AI Operating Modes

Declare the primary mode in PRE-FLIGHT: **READ-ONLY AUDIT**, **WRITE/FIX**, **PROPOSE ONLY**, or **QUARANTINE BEFORE DELETE**.

| Mode | PRE-FLIGHT required | May write files |
|---|---|---|
| READ-ONLY AUDIT | Yes | No |
| WRITE/FIX | Yes | Yes (whitelist) |
| PROPOSE ONLY | Yes | No |
| QUARANTINE BEFORE DELETE | Yes | No (mark only) |

READ-ONLY AUDIT must deliver findings P0–P3 and whitelist/blacklist without stopping for debt alone.

WRITE/FIX requires strict stop conditions, validation matrix, and selective git staging.

PROPOSE ONLY delivers proposed changes and waits for human authorization.

QUARANTINE BEFORE DELETE documents deletion candidates; no direct deletes in the same phase.

## Required PRE-FLIGHT CHECKLIST

Before modifying any file, output a visible block:

**PRE-FLIGHT CHECKLIST**

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| task scope | One sentence describing the authorized work |
| operating mode | READ-ONLY AUDIT / WRITE/FIX / PROPOSE ONLY / QUARANTINE BEFORE DELETE |
| files allowed | Explicit list |
| files forbidden | Explicit list including src, backend, tests, blindaje v1 files if applicable |
| module in scope | Single module or docs-only |
| modules out of scope | All other modules |
| source-of-truth | Which registry, API, table, or golden file applies |
| Golden Dataset requirement | yes/no; which dataset IDs |
| legacy/duplicate check | Planned search strategy |
| test oracle check | Which tests must pass; no weakening allowed |
| security/multi-tenant impact | yes/no; summary |
| stop conditions | Which apply to this task |
| why this approach is safe | Concise justification |

Do not expose private chain-of-thought. Provide only the checklist and a concise reasoning summary.

## Reasoning Summary Rule

Allowed in responses:

- concise reasoning summary
- explicit assumptions labelled Assumed / Pending C.13 validation
- verification evidence (commands run, files read)
- risk classification P0/P1/P2/P3
- decisions needing human review

Forbidden:

- claiming Confirmed without audit evidence
- certifying legal/financial/compliance outcomes
- hiding uncertainty behind confident language

## Patch Discipline

- No placeholders (`// ... existing code ...`, `omitted for brevity`, etc.)
- No broad refactor outside scope
- No adjacent cleanup ("while I'm here")
- No unrequested formatting sweeps
- No weakening tests or golden expected values
- No wrapping full repository files in Markdown code fences when writing `.mdc`, `.md`, `.cursorignore`, or `AGENTS.md`
- Complete blocks when code change is authorized

## Plain Text File Writing Rule

When writing `.mdc`, `.md`, `.cursorignore`, or `AGENTS.md` to disk:

- File must start with real content (frontmatter `---` for `.mdc`)
- Do not wrap entire file in triple-backtick fences
- Inline code examples inside docs are allowed when teaching format

## Required Final Summary

End every execution phase with:

| Section | Content |
|---|---|
| what was checked | Files, commands, registries |
| what changed | Only if authorized; else "none" |
| why | Risk reduced or documentation purpose |
| risks reduced | Specific risks |
| what was not touched | Explicit list |
| validation run | Commands and outcomes |
| docs reconciliation | Which docs changed vs intentionally unchanged |
| remaining risks | Open P0/P1/P2/P3 |
| next step | Recommended prompt or phase |
| demo/pilot status | demo-ready / partial / not ready |

## Handoff Trigger

After completing a phase/subphase, or when context is long, generate HANDOFF_STATE per AGENTS.md and AI_OPERATING_MODEL.md.

## Stop Conditions

Mode-aware policy applies.

**READ-ONLY AUDIT:** stop only if pre-flight cannot be completed honestly, task requires forbidden writes, or real secrets are exposed. Do not stop for audit findings alone.

**WRITE/FIX / QUARANTINE follow-up:** stop before modifying if pre-flight cannot be completed honestly, or if task requires forbidden files without authorization.
